@schema agentdocs/v1
@id ugui-html-export-feasibility
@title "uGUI RectTransform-to-HTML Export"
@kind exploration
@description
DeedPlanner can export an active uGUI RectTransform subtree as a portable, scalable HTML fragment bundle. The exporter is Editor-only, read-only against the hierarchy, and independent of any document host.
@end-description

@decisions
@decision id=D1 status=locked by=human layout=full
@question
What does the first exporter preserve?
@end-question
@selected id=A format=markdown title="Retained RectTransforms, rendered images, and basic text"
Export the retained RectTransform hierarchy as nested HTML, render every Unity `Image` and `RawImage` to real PNG-backed `<img>` elements, and include TMP labels as editable HTML text with a browser fallback font.
@end-selected
@end-decision
@decision id=D2 status=locked by=human layout=full
@question
What is the output contract?
@end-question
@selected id=A format=markdown title="Generic composable directory bundle"
Write one scoped `index.html` fragment, `manifest.json`, and deduplicated PNG files under `assets/`. The artifact works from disk, any local web server, or a document system that accepts relative assets; the exporter performs no upload and has no AgentDocs dependency.
@end-selected
@end-decision
@decision id=D3 status=locked by=human layout=full
@question
How do humans and agents invoke it?
@end-question
@selected id=A format=markdown title="Editor selection and Pipeline object reference"
Humans use **DeedPlanner > Export Selected UI as HTML** for either an active hierarchy root or a prefab selected in the Project window. Agents call `ui_export_html` with a scene-object or prefab-asset reference and an empty output directory.
@end-selected
@end-decision
@end-decisions

@risks
@risk id=R1 kind=edge-case severity=1 tests=T1
@description
Coordinate conversion can drift through pivots, nested scale, or Z rotation.
@end-description
@end-risk
@risk id=R2 kind=edge-case severity=1 tests=T2
@description
Sliced, tiled, filled, tinted, and sprite-less Images can differ if their browser representation reimplements Unity rendering.
@end-description
@end-risk
@risk id=R3 kind=general severity=1 tests=T3
@description
Unsupported visual components can make an export incomplete without making that limitation visible.
@end-description
@end-risk
@end-risks

@tests
@test id=T1 tester=unit status=success
@description
Parent-relative top-left coordinates, proportional values, scale, and Z rotation retain their resolved geometry.
@end-description
@method
EditMode tests compare known RectTransform fixtures with the exporter geometry, including a rotated child, retained layout-only ancestors, and omitted empty leaves.
@end-method
@end-test
@test id=T2 tester=unit status=success
@description
Unity Images and RawImages become valid, deduplicated PNG assets with real rendered pixels.
@end-description
@method
EditMode tests decode generated Image and cropped RawImage PNGs and export the real `Deed Card.prefab` in its initialized no-thumbnail state, verifying that its inactive RawImage is omitted while sliced Images and TMP labels remain.
@end-method
@end-test
@test id=T3 tester=unit status=success
@description
Unsupported visuals and approximation boundaries are reported in the result and manifest.
@end-description
@method
Tests cover RectMask2D warnings; the exporter also reports masks, mesh effects, custom Image or RawImage materials, unsupported Graphics, out-of-plane rotation, and fallback TMP fonts.
@end-method
@end-test
@end-tests

@section format=markdown title="Artifact Contract"
The output directory contains:

```text
index.html
manifest.json
assets/
  image-name-contenthash.png
```

`index.html` is intentionally an HTML fragment rather than a document shell. A browser renders it directly, while another document can compose its scoped styles and `.ugui-export` root without removing document-shell wrappers. The current contract is `ugui-html-export/v2`.

The root records its exact source width and height and uses the same aspect ratio at any display width. Each retained RectTransform is a nested `.ugui-export__rect` whose geometry is relative to its retained parent. `manifest.json` records the same `rects` parent graph plus the visual `elements`. DOM order follows uGUI traversal order.
@end-section

@section format=markdown title="Rendering Rules"
The exporter forces Canvas and layout updates before sampling the active hierarchy. A RectTransform is retained when it has a supported visual or is an ancestor needed to connect one to the selected root. Empty visual-less leaves and behavior components are excluded. This makes the result a composable mosaic of nested layout pieces rather than a flattened screenshot.

Every visible `Image` or `RawImage` is rendered in isolation at its resolved size. This preserves Simple, Sliced, Tiled, and Filled Images as well as RawImage UV cropping, texture sampling, tint, alpha, preserve-aspect behavior, and sprite-less colored panels without changing texture importer settings. Identical PNG bytes share one content-hashed asset.

TMP labels remain editable HTML text. Basic alignment, size, color, bold, italic, underline, and strikethrough are retained. TMP font assets are not embedded, so the fragment uses Arial as its explicit fallback and records the Unity font name as metadata.
@end-section

@section format=markdown title="Boundaries"
Active scene and Prefab Mode targets export their current resolved state. A prefab asset can also be exported directly: the command loads its root into an isolated Prefab stage, resolves its serialized layout, exports it, and unloads it without saving changes. Direct prefab export requires a RectTransform root with a positive intrinsic size.

Direct prefab export does not run `Awake`, presenters, or other runtime initialization. Dynamic widgets therefore export their serialized prefab state; agents should use an initialized scene instance when the intended state depends on runtime data.

Mask and RectMask2D clipping, custom mesh effects, arbitrary Graphics, custom Image or RawImage materials, and out-of-plane transforms are not reproduced. Each visible occurrence produces an explicit warning instead of being silently approximated. Interaction, animation, scripts, layout behavior, and other non-visual components are excluded.

The output directory must be absent or empty. This prevents the exporter from deleting or overwriting unrelated files and prevents stale assets from entering a later bundle upload.
@end-section

@section format=markdown title="AgentDocs Compatibility"
AgentDocs can consume the directory with `vault add <directory>`, but that is only one optional downstream workflow. DeedPlanner writes ordinary files and relative URLs and neither calls nor detects AgentDocs.
@end-section
